# iLoveMD - Environment Variables Example
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development

# =============================================================================
# DEVELOPMENT API KEYS (Optional)
# =============================================================================

# None needed. Users enter their own API keys in the UI.

# Shared secret for signing free-mode (Modal) access tokens. Must match the
# ilovemd-modal-token Modal secret. Needed to use free mode against the deployed
# Modal app; without it the deployed app rejects requests.
# MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=

# =============================================================================
# DEVELOPMENT VARIABLES
# =============================================================================
# Add any development-specific environment variables below

# Example: Custom API endpoint for development
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Example: Enable debug mode
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEBUG=true

# =============================================================================
# PRODUCTION NOTES
# =============================================================================
# For production deployment on Vercel, no environment variables are required.
# The application is designed to work without server-side configuration.
#
# Privacy-first design:
# - No API keys stored server-side
# - No user data collected or stored
# - Page views are counted with Vercel Web Analytics (no cookies)
# - All processing done client-side (except PDF conversion proxy)
